invariant: INV-16
file: record.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_host
reason: the record layer runs every record's Poly1305 on the decomposition
  whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu states, so a caller that stated the
  multiply's timing gets the slow copy on every record and the bit picks
  nothing there. The tags are the same. test/tcp_blocking_loop_widemul.h
  requires a handshake between two ends whose ch_cfg.cpu holds
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY to call no file under its own names.

--- old
    return d->widemul;
--- new
    (void)d;
    return WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED;
